#!/bin/bash
source /home/anaconda3/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
conda activate glod-ris
unset CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
cd /home/msj_team/Jacob/research/ris
SESSION_FILE=/home/msj_team/Jacob/research/ris/aris-sota.session
LOG=/home/msj_team/Jacob/research/ris/aris-sota.log
STAMP=/home/msj_team/Jacob/research/ris/extreme_started.txt
SOTA_STAMP=/home/msj_team/Jacob/research/ris/sota_bar_started.txt
[ -f "$STAMP" ] || touch "$STAMP"
[ -f "$SOTA_STAMP" ] || touch "$SOTA_STAMP"

START_PROMPT=$(cat <<'EOF'
/research-pipeline "Beat published SOTA on every RIS validation set" — AUTO_PROCEED: true, auto_write: false, venue: CVPR, difficulty: hard, code review: false, render html: false, compact: true, base repo: https://github.com/fhgyuanshen/HybridGL

This run does not end when a reviewer scores 6/10 or says almost, and it does not end at MAX_ROUNDS=4. Those skill defaults are overridden. auto_write is false on purpose. The current paper is rejected: its best RefCOCO-family numbers are 55.58 / 46.03 / 51.00 mIoU against GLOD-RIS 58.42 / 54.01 / 57.85, and gRefCOCO at 23.11 cIoU / 20.67 gIoU is not a published SOTA. Do not polish that draft. Do not call /paper-writing until python3 extreme_bar.py prints PASS.

Read RESEARCH_BRIEF.md. Do not redo the literature survey. The old gated-growth result stays dead. If a one-line control explains a gain, kill that method, record it, and design a different one. Repeat until a method still leads after those controls.

Required before any submission draft, all newer than extreme_started.txt:
- exp/out_final/main_refcoco.json, main_refcocoplus.json, main_refcocog.json, main_grefcoco.json with n >= 10834, 10758, 4896, 2000. These are four full validation sets: RefCOCO, RefCOCO+, RefCOCOg, and gRefCOCO. Download gRefCOCO. Fewer than four datasets does not pass.
- exp/out_final/sota_table.json: {"methods": [...]} length >= 6. Each measured_by_us true row needs an evidence path. At least 3 methods must be run here, not copied from papers.
- exp/out_final/ablation.json: {"rows": [...]} length >= 5, each with an evidence path from a real run.
- refine-logs/METHOD_GRAVEYARD.md with at least two killed methods.
- exp/out_final/protocol_audit.json: cross-paper metric-protocol consistency (operator instruction 2026-10-08). Every shipped number and every cross-paper comparison must use the SAME metric protocol as the published numbers compared against. Audit all four datasets, gRefCOCO first: identify the exact protocol the compared papers use (official benchmark eval code where cited; for gRefCOCO the official evaluation, including the no-target treatment and which records enter each average), re-evaluate the saved predictions under it, and record per dataset: protocol_source, definition, aligned: true, plus the numbers after alignment. If alignment changes any number, update the main jsons, sota_table.json, and the paper tables and shipped lines --- the aligned numbers stand even if weaker. Document the protocol in the paper. Rebuild paper/main.pdf AFTER writing the audit (the gate checks the PDF is newer).
- exp/out_final/sensitivity.json, stability.json, complexity.json (user instruction 2026-10-09): parameter-sensitivity sweeps, stability tests, and model-complexity accounting (parameters, FLOPs per query, peak memory, latency; training_time states explicitly that nothing is trained and reports the selector-fitting cost). The SOTA table must carry both mIoU and oIoU for every RefCOCO-family row. Rebuild paper/main.pdf after these files (the bar gates them).
- paper/figures/architecture.pdf or .svg from /figure-spec, at least 20 KB. Not a matplotlib sketch.
- A CVPR paper with \appendix, then paper/main.pdf.
- Full-line SOTA, written into each main json as "shipped" after sota_bar_started.txt. RefCOCO, RefCOCO+, and RefCOCOg shipped.mIoU must be strictly greater than shipped.best_published.mIoU, and best_published.mIoU must be at least 58.42, 54.01, and 57.85. For gRefCOCO the comparison is same-methodology (operator instruction 2026-10-08): shipped.cIoU and shipped.gIoU must strictly beat shipped.best_published from the same method class, and the same-class published floors are at least 42.0 cIoU and 43.3 gIoU (PSALM zero-shot on gRefCOCO val, ECCV 2024 Table 12). Fully-supervised methods (InstAlign 68.94/74.34, GSVA(ft), ReLA) are reference rows in a separate labelled table, never the floor. A little supervision is allowed for gRefCOCO: a small component (e.g. a selector head, not a full supervised segmenter) may be trained on the gRefCOCO train split, tuned only on a held-out split carved from train, official val/test kept evaluation-only; declare trained-vs-frozen in the json and the paper. If a newer same-class paper is higher, raise best_published and beat that. Beating the reproduced HybridGL row is not SOTA. A method that loses any one dataset is killed.
If the current architecture misses any dataset, run Optuna for at least 300 completed trials before changing the architecture. The search objective is a held-out split, never the official validation or test split used for the SOTA claim. Write the study to exp/out_final/optuna_study.json with n_trials and the best params. If 300 trials still miss any dataset, change the model, record the failed architecture in the graveyard, and start a new study of at least 300 trials. Do not write the paper during a study.
python3 extreme_bar.py must print PASS. Until then, keep experimenting.

Use conda env glod-ris. Do not download PyTorch from download.pytorch.org. Reuse RefCOCO data already on disk. All 4 GPUs are available; check nvidia-smi and do not kill other users or the RVOS job. Do not call Codex. Reviews go to mcp__llm-chat__review with executor_model deepseek-flash. Record the reviewer as glm-5.3. Version control (user instruction 2026-10-10): this project is mirrored to a private GitHub backup --- bash backup.sh commits and pushes, and accepts a message (bash backup.sh "milestone: ..."). At every meaningful milestone --- a new shipped result, an acceptance-gate PASS, a paper revision, a major experiment concluded, or before any risky or large change --- run it so the history marks the milestone and a rollback point exists. Keep it append-only: never rewrite history or run destructive git operations; older versions are retrieved read-only via git log / git show. A periodic sidecar also snapshots every 30 minutes.
Component-provenance escalation (operator directive 2026-10-15; the model's bulk must be components this run proposed): the head's measured attribution shows the released HybridGL quantities are load-bearing, not a guardrail --- box-over-full-pool scores 50.20/40.24/49.48 mIoU while box within the released scores' top-k restriction reaches 68.53/64.67/65.12 (drop-one deltas: restriction +18.3/+24.4/+15.6 given the box; box +25.2/+26.8/+17.6 given the restriction), so an adversarial read could call the shipped pipeline "HybridGL plus a box". Measure that and fix it, do not reword it away. Deliverables: (1) exp/out_final/component_provenance.json accounting for EVERY shipped component (name, role, provenance in {ours, released_hybridgl, generic_frozen}, evidence path); (2) a head-rebuild study re-measuring the candidate-restriction stage from OUR OWN mechanisms, all as deterministic re-analysis over the cached records (no vision re-generation needed): arm family A --- our own region-text protocol score (generic masked-region CLIP with the FULL sentence, the protocol this run established; no released ensemble, no GEM term) as the top-k key; arm family B --- geometric self-consistency guards only (box-fill fraction, center-in-box, area-ratio-to-box, containment), no text scoring; arm family C --- combinations or learned heads over our own terms (declare anything fitted); the released-restriction+box configuration stays as the reference arm; evaluate every arm on the three full official val splits under the aligned protocol and report the deltas against both the reference arm and the released end-to-end pipeline; (3) if an ours-only arm holds parity or better, promote it into the shipped head, update the method section, ablation table, abstract and the provenance table (add it to the paper appendix) so the shipped pipeline's decisive components are all ours and HybridGL appears only as the platform/baseline row, and rebuild the paper; if no ours-only arm reaches parity, the verdict must state the measured gap and the framing must publish BOTH drop-one deltas so the conjunction (released scores narrow the instance class; our box picks the instance) is the honest, clearly attributed claim --- under no circumstances may the paper's wording understate the released scores' measured contribution. The bar gates exp/out_final/component_provenance.json (components[] >= 8 with non-empty name/role/evidence and provenance in {ours, released_hybridgl, generic_frozen}; head_rebuild.arms[] >= 2, each with name, uses_released_scores bool, fresh evidence, and val{refcoco, refcocoplus, refcocog} floats, at least one arm with uses_released_scores=false; non-empty verdict; paper/main.pdf rebuilt after it).
Backbone-strength audit (operator directive 2026-10-16; the contribution must not be attributable to stronger or more backbones than the rivals'): the shipped lineup is SAM ViT-H + CLIP ViT-B/16 + LLaVA-OneVision-7B + GroundingDINO-base (gRefCOCO path only) + a small learned head, and the limitations section itself admits "other generators and backbones were not varied". The "not stronger" side is already evidenced (glm_mllm_swap.json: SOTA holds with GLOD-RIS's exact MLLM, deltas -0.95/-1.07/-2.00 mIoU and still far above their published rows; the SigLIP-so400m probe: a stronger encoder selects worse; points_per_side 8->16: the diagnosis survives). Now measure the STRICTLY WEAKER side so the paper can claim "fewer/weaker backbones than the rival, still SOTA". Arms, each under a deployment-consistent head (refit the learned head on train-carved rows for any changed feature platform, declared; the training-free realization may serve directly), on the full official val splits under the aligned protocol, reported against the GLOD-RIS published floors (58.42/54.01/57.85 mIoU; for gRefCOCO the same-class floors and our own record): (a) a strictly smaller local VLM in place of LLaVA-OneVision-7B (3B class or smaller; strictly smaller than both the incumbent and the rival's cloud MLLM) re-extracting boxes on the full val sets; (b) a smaller SAM (ViT-L and/or ViT-B, both strictly weaker than the rival's ViT-H) regenerating the proposal pool; (c) a weaker region-text platform for the head's scoring terms (CLIP ViT-B/32, or plain masked-region features without the released complement-blur path); (d) gRefCOCO without the extra GroundingDINO detector (fewer components than the rival). If an arm drops below the floors, that drop is the measured boundary --- report it and keep the arm. Write exp/out_final/backbone_audit.json (inventory[] >= 4 of the shipped lineup with name/params/role/provenance; swaps[] >= 4 arms with name, component, weaker_variant, fresh evidence, val{} numeric results, still_sota bool, at least 3 distinct components across arms; a verdict stating plainly whether SOTA holds with a strictly weaker/fewer lineup than the rival's; paper/main.pdf rebuilt after it) and fold the result into the paper's complexity and limitations sections. The bar gates the file. Box re-extraction and pool regeneration are expected GPU work; prefer caches where valid; budget discipline stands.
Framing correction (operator directive 2026-10-17; applies to every subsequent paper rebuild and review): do NOT present the GLOD-RIS reproduction shortfall as a finding or criticism of their method --- with no released code the shortfall cannot be attributed to them and is not a defect of their work; a reviewer can always counter "your reimplementation is wrong", and the criticism invites symmetric attack. Re-aim every place it currently reads as criticism (abstract, intro, sota ledger, section titles): state it neutrally as a comparison-protocol note --- GLOD-RIS releases no code; our faithful end-to-end reimplementation of the described method does not reach its published numbers; therefore every comparison quotes their published rows as published (cross-harness, explicitly labelled), and the reproduction, its provenance and its unaccounted remainder are documented transparently in the appendix, without judging the original work. The rule-swap stays as a controlled measurement of the described guidance ("under our reading of the published equations") described neutrally --- never as "their rule is harmful". The narrative driver of the diagnosis section must be our own measurements (oracle decomposition, wrong-instance taxonomy, encoder probe), which never depended on their reproduction. Keep every number unchanged and visible: this is a framing change only, not a retraction.
Minimal-configuration follow-up (operator directive 2026-10-17): the existing attribution arms already show the RefCOCO family holds SOTA on two frozen models only --- box-fill over the full pool (69.99/65.22/64.83) and the geometric-guard variants (69.70/64.95/64.83), all above the published GLOD-RIS row (58.42/54.01/57.85) with NO CLIP platform, NO detector and NO training. (1) Add the missing gRefCOCO arm: the learned head with LLaVA nounboxes only and NO GroundingDINO --- the training-free no-detector arm currently falls to 38.71, below the 42.0 floor; if the learned-head variant also fails, that is the measured boundary and stays declared. (2) Promote the minimal configuration to a first-class named result: an ablation row plus a paragraph ("minimal configuration: one segmenter + one frozen VLM, no CLIP platform, no detector, no training, still above every published same-class number on the RefCOCO family") folded into the backbone-audit artifact and the next paper rebuild --- do not change the shipped configuration; this is a positioning claim backed by the existing arms, not a new shipped method.
No-detector gRefCOCO rescue (operator directive 2026-10-17; answers "can zero-shot SOTA be reached without the detector"): the training-free no-detector arm measures cIoU 38.71 against the 44.4 same-class floor (its gIoU 69.69 and N-acc 86.17 clear their floors --- the detector is load-bearing for cIoU only). Before accepting that boundary, run the untested rescue arms for the ZERO-SHOT no-detector path with the cached-records machinery: (a) upgrade the per-term boxes from LLaVA noun prompts to the per-clause FULL text --- the full-sentence-over-noun-phrase finding this run established (+13.4/+10.6/+11.6) was never applied to the gRefCOCO term path (history shows only paraphrase variants p2/p3 and detector substitutes); (b) presence-verified term filtering --- drop hallucinated terms per clause using the existing presence machinery on the no-detector configuration; (c) the union/pair candidate family with the no-detector boxes. Report the best no-detector zero-shot cIoU/gIoU/N-acc and whether the cIoU floor clears; if none clears it, the measured boundary stands as the documented answer (with-detector zero-shot 51.32 SOTA; no-detector zero-shot SOTA on gIoU and N-acc only, cIoU 38.71 stated). Also complete the learned-head no-detector arm already queued (declared-trained, not zero-shot). Fold every outcome into the backbone-audit artifact and the next paper rebuild.
GroundingDINO removal + rival-aligned VLM (operator directive 2026-10-18, supersedes the queued rescue where they differ): (1) DELETE GroundingDINO from the gRefCOCO path. The RefCOCO family already runs on two frozen models (SAM + VLM) and gRefCOCO must do the same --- replace the detector's term-level boxes with box sources already in the pipeline (per-clause VLM prompts; after alignment GLM-4.1V; same clause machinery) and rebuild the gRefCOCO selection accordingly. Target: clear the same-class floor (cIoU >= 44.4) and report the measured cost against the current record (52.71 cIoU) honestly; if the naive DINO-free arms miss, run an AGGRESSIVE hyperparameter search (>= 300 completed trials, objective on held-out/train-carved rows ONLY --- never official val) over the DINO-free rule/head (term-box construction, clause prompt form, picker weights, abstention thresholds), and try the learned acceptance prior on VLM-only term boxes. Write exp/out_final/gref_nodetector.json (arms[] >= 2 with name, boxes_source, val.cIoU, val.gIoU, val.N_acc, still_sota, fresh evidence; if no arm is SOTA, a search{} block with n_trials >= 300 and best_params; verdict; paper rebuilt after) --- the bar gates it. If a DINO-free arm ships, update the shipped gRefCOCO row, the component inventory (14 -> 13) and the paper. (2) ALIGN THE BOX VLM WITH GLOD-RIS: use GLM-4.1V-Thinking-Flash (Zhipu API, the rival's exact MLLM) as the box source for the RefCOCO family on the FULL official val splits --- not the earlier 2,000-sample subset; cache every response; refit the learned head and the reference on train-carved rows with GLM boxes wherever the box source changed; report GLM-box and LLaVA-box results side by side. This makes the comparison component-matched end to end (same segmenter, same CLIP, same MLLM), so neither the backbone family nor the API can be raised as the source of our margin. Write exp/out_final/glm_aligned.json (model string naming the GLM model; datasets{refcoco,refcocoplus,refcocog} each with n above the full-split floors, mIoU, oIoU, llava_mIoU; verdict; paper rebuilt after) --- the bar gates it. Budget: full val is ~26.5k expressions, ~3 h at the recorded 2.2-2.5 q/s with modest concurrency; cache everything and reuse existing GLM caches where valid. The Qwen2.5-VL-3B finding stays a separate audit arm.
Literature-coverage expansion (operator directive 2026-10-18; the advisor asked how many papers are actually cited): the paper currently carries 17 bibliography entries (~10 RIS) and the compared-method table lists PSALM, SELF1E, LAVT, ReLA, SAM4MLLM and InstAlign with NO bibliography entries at all --- that is a real gap, and the advisor's bar is >20 works with >= 15 RIS. Expand the bibliography and Related Work using ONLY works whose identifiers are verified (arXiv ID or DOI): reuse NOVELTY_DOSSIER.md's verified list (MARS, E-SAM, ProposalCLIP, RefChess, PinPoint, Venice-H1, RAS, S+S, Tarot-SAM3, GFR-SAM, RefAM, IteRPrime, GSVA, LoTeR, ...) and add the formal citations for every compared method (PSALM, SELF1E, LAVT, ReLA, SAM4MLLM, InstAlign, GRES, GLOD-RIS, HybridGL, TAS, BMS, LGD, Ref-Diff, MaskCLIP, Global-Local, IteRPrime) with \cite on every method row of every comparison table. Verify each new entry via the arXiv API / DOI resolution; never fabricate authors, venues, years or identifiers; if a field cannot be verified, write it as unavailable rather than guessing. Target: >= 30 bibliography entries with >= 15 RIS/same-class works among them, each discussed or cited where relevant. Write exp/out_final/literature_coverage.json (references[] >= 15 with key, title, identifier --- identifier must match an arXiv or DOI pattern; every key must exist in paper/references.bib; verdict; paper rebuilt after) --- the bar gates it. Do not change any experimental number.
Deep literature reading (operator directive 2026-10-18; the advisor's bar is READ THROUGH >= 20 papers in FULL TEXT, > 15 of them RIS --- abstract-level verification no longer suffices): build a structured deep-read dossier. Local corpus: 17 PDFs already in papers/ (GLOD-RIS, HybridGL, TAS, BMS, IteRPrimE, LGD, RefDiff, RAS, CaR, MCCE-REC and others); download the missing ones (PSALM, SELF1E, LAVT, ReLA, SAM4MLLM, InstAlign, GRES, RefChess, PinPoint, Venice-H1, MARS, E-SAM, ProposalCLIP, GF-SAM as needed). For EVERY paper: read the full text (not the abstract) and record (a) the method mechanism with section/equation anchors, (b) the paper's reported numbers on the benchmarks we share (>= 2 numeric entries per paper), (c) exactly what it does differently from us, (d) a novelty-threat verdict, (e) one verbatim key quote. Write exp/out_final/deep_read.json (papers[] >= 20; each with key --- must exist in references.bib ---, title, identifier (arXiv/DOI), category in {ris, adjacent}, depth="full-text", method, claims, reported_numbers{} >= 2 numerics, relation, threat, key_quote, anchors[] >= 2; category=ris count >= 15; verdict; paper rebuilt after) --- the bar gates it. If a full text is unobtainable, say so and substitute another RIS paper rather than downgrading to an abstract. Fold the reading into the Related Work positioning (what each family does, what we change) and keep every citation identifier-verified; never fabricate authors, venues, years or numbers. Do not change any experimental number or claim.
Paper-download + source-code inspection (operator directive 2026-10-18): every deep-read paper must be downloaded as the ORIGINAL full text into papers/ (arXiv PDF or publisher PDF) and read from that local copy --- record its path as source_file in exp/out_final/deep_read.json and answer questions from the PDF, not from memory. Where a method's code is public (GitHub), download or clone it and inspect the implementation where it matters --- constants and defaults, training/eval protocol, metric conventions --- and record code{available, repo, inspected, findings} per paper; at least 3 papers must carry code-level findings, including at least one gRefCOCO method (PSALM/GRES/ReLA/SAM4MLLM/InstAlign -- whichever has a runnable repo) to verify the metric conventions of the gRefCOCO comparison; HybridGL's already-reproduced implementation counts. Methods with no public code (GLOD-RIS) record available=false explicitly. Never fabricate a repo or findings.
Source-code consumption (operator directive 2026-10-18; "inspect as many repos as possible and RUN them"): enumerate every compared method (PSALM, GRES, LAVT, ReLA, SAM4MLLM, InstAlign, RefChess, MARS, E-SAM, ProposalCLIP, GF-SAM, RAS, GLOD-RIS, HybridGL, TAS, BMS, LGD, Ref-Diff, MaskCLIP, Global-Local, IteRPrime); clone every public repo (record URL + commit), inspect the implementation where it matters (constants/defaults, training/eval protocol, metric conventions), and RUN every runnable repo with its released checkpoints on a small official sample (>= 100 expressions; full splits only where cheap), recording entry point, sample_n, status and sample metrics in code.run. Full reproductions follow the standing discipline (no tuning on val; env/weight/license blockers documented precisely count as attempted, not as runs). Minimums the bar enforces: >= 8 inspected repos, >= 5 successful runs, and the gRefCOCO metric convention verified in code and recorded as grefcoco_metric_check{method, repo, finding}. HybridGL is already reproduced; InstAlign's repo is a placeholder and GLOD-RIS has no code -- record available=false. Never fabricate a repo, run or result.
DINO-free gRefCOCO, search until it works (operator directive 2026-10-20; the deletion is non-negotiable): GroundingDINO must leave the gRefCOCO path and stay out. The current DINO-free best is 40.55 cIoU after a 320-trial search (floor 44.4); continue WITHOUT a trial cap until a DINO-free arm clears the same-class floors (cIoU >= 44.4 AND gIoU >= 43.3) and becomes the shipped gRefCOCO row. The search space is NOT limited to hyperparameters --- redesign any component of the DINO-free path; the operator explicitly allows changing other things: term decomposition and clause parsing; box source (full-expression VLM; per-clause VLM with Qwen2.5-VL-3B --- measured better than the 7B family on the family tables; dense-CLIP / MaskCLIP term heatmaps localized to boxes; SAM point prompts from VLM evidence); candidate construction (multi-mask/union, MMNet-style multiple outputs, pair/union); per-term verification (presence probes, yes-no, 2AFC, Set-of-Mark term selection); the learned head over VLM/dense-CLIP term features; abstention. The frozen backbones (SAM/CLIP/VLM weights) stay frozen. Discipline: every configuration tuned on held-out/train-carved rows only; ONE official pass per frozen configuration; record every attempt (config, tune numbers, official numbers where evaluated) in the search ledger; if an arm clears the floors, ship it as the DINO-free gRefCOCO row, update main_grefcoco.json, the component inventory (13 components), and the paper, and report the delta against the detector-bearing 50.34/74.69. The deep-read dossier points the way: TAS-style text augmentation, MaskCLIP dense labels, MMNet multi-mask, per-term VLM selection, Qwen2.5-VL-3B boxes. The bar gate now REQUIRES a DINO-free arm with still_sota=true and shipped_detector_free=true; the previous search-block escape is removed --- effort alone no longer passes.
Reproduction framing, final removal (operator directive 2026-10-20): the operator's position --- a published result is assumed valid in its authors' environment; our inability to reproduce without released code is not evidence about their work and must never be raised as a finding. Remove the reproduction shortfall from the abstract and the introduction entirely (no 20-26 numbers, no "below the published rows", no such framing anywhere in the main narrative); the main text may state only the neutral comparison protocol --- code unreleased -> published rows quoted as published, cross-harness labelled. Keep the independent reimplementation and its unaccounted remainder ONLY as a transparency record in the appendix, written without judgment. Remove the independent-reproduction row from the main SOTA table (it lives in the appendix record). Keep every number in the evidence artifacts. The rule-swap stays only as a controlled measurement "under our reading of the published equations", never as evidence against the original work. Rebuild the paper.
Multi-pipeline diagnosis (operator directive 2026-10-20; answers "you only looked at one baseline"): the direct oracle-gap decomposition currently exists for ONE released pipeline (HybridGL) plus our own; the rest of the field is covered only by the paradigm argument and published numbers. Repeat the SAME diagnosis on at least TWO additional RELEASED same-class zero-shot pipelines, each with its own pool and its own selection, on the full official val split or a stated uniform sample: Global-Local (Seonghoon-Yu/Zero-shot-RIS, code inspected in the dossier) and at least one more runnable (TAS / Ref-Diff / a MaskCLIP-based pipeline; the GLOD-RIS reproduction counts as one pipeline where cached selections exist). For each pipeline report: pool oracle mIoU over its own pool, achieved mIoU/oIoU, the gap taxonomy under the same classifier (wrong-instance share of the gap MASS), n, and evidence. The claim under test: every score-based selection sits far below its own pool oracle and the gap is dominated by wrong-instance selection --- if any pipeline violates this, report it honestly; that would bound the paradigm claim. Write exp/out_final/multipipeline_diagnosis.json (pipelines[] >= 2, each with name, n, oracle, achieved, wrong_instance_share, evidence; verdict; paper rebuilt after) and fold one row per pipeline into the diagnosis section. The bar gates it.
Full reproductions only (operator directive 2026-10-20): every reproduction we undertake must be COMPLETE --- full official validation split, official evaluation protocol, released weights, no sampling, no reduced-scope arms. A top-venue paper is not reproduced by a 5-record metric check or a 100-expression sample. For the multi-pipeline diagnosis this means: each reproduced pipeline runs on the full official val splits (refcoco 10,834 / refcocoplus 10,758 / refcocog 4,896; gRefCOCO 14,229 where applicable) under the official evaluation, with the achieved metric, its own pool oracle and the gap taxonomy computed on the full population. Sampling is permitted only when a split's full evaluation is impossible for a documented reason (e.g., server-side scoring); then use the largest public population and state the blocker. Methods whose code or released weights are genuinely unobtainable are documented as blocked with evidence --- not sampled. Schema update for exp/out_final/multipipeline_diagnosis.json: each pipeline reports datasets{<name>: {n, oracle, achieved, wrong_instance_share}} with every reported dataset at full-split n, evidence and notes.
Sustained operation (operator directive 2026-10-20): this is a multi-day run; the operator expects the pipeline to stay busy with real work for days, not to stop or idle. Most of the work is waiting --- keep every wait INSIDE the turn (the longest single waits, or a background wait that notifies on completion), batch the status checks, and never end a turn without real progress. Run every gate to completion: full-split reproductions, the DINO-free search, the multi-pipeline diagnosis; when a job finishes, immediately queue the next experiment. Do not spin-poll, do not re-conclude the same failure, do not stop early. The anti-spin guard exists only for degenerate loops (three consecutive sub-60s no-work cycles).
Independent full reproductions (operator directive 2026-10-20, follow-up to the full-reproduction standard): the multi-pipeline diagnosis currently rests on the two pipelines we already had (HybridGL, GLOD-RIS). Add at least TWO additional independent released same-class pipelines beyond those two --- Global-Local (Zero-shot-RIS, CVPR 2023) first, then TAS / Ref-Diff / MaskCLIP-based where code and released weights are obtainable --- each on the FULL official val splits under the official protocol, with its own pool oracle, achieved metric and wrong-instance share. Methods whose code or weights are genuinely unobtainable get a precise documented blocker with evidence, and at least ONE new pipeline must deliver full-split numbers. Update exp/out_final/multipipeline_diagnosis.json: every pipeline carries its repo URL; the file must contain >= 2 new-pipeline entries (full results or documented blockers) beyond the HybridGL/GLOD-RIS pair, and update the paper diagnosis table with one row per new pipeline.
Protocol alignment per reproduction (operator directive 2026-10-20): published numbers can come from different experimental protocols --- split versions, metric definitions (mIoU vs pooled oIoU, J vs J&F, cIoU/gIoU aggregation, per-sentence vs per-ref grouping, no-target and empty-mask conventions), and evaluation harnesses (server-scored vs public GT). That protocol variance is exactly why every method must be reproduced individually. For every reproduced pipeline: record its exact protocol, re-evaluate it under OUR unified official protocol, and report its published numbers and our reproduction side by side together with every protocol difference found. The diagnosis and comparison tables must be single-protocol; any side that cannot be aligned is stated explicitly, never silently pooled. Schema: each pipeline in exp/out_final/multipipeline_diagnosis.json carries protocol (string) and published (per-dataset numbers, or an explicit note that the published number is not comparable).
EOF
